# sdist-only inclusions. The wheel picks these up via
# [tool.setuptools.package-data] in pyproject.toml; setuptools' default
# sdist heuristics skip non-Python files at the package root unless we
# spell them out here.
#
# Why every file is listed explicitly:
#   - README.md is referenced via ``readme = "README.md"`` in
#     pyproject.toml and setuptools auto-includes it. Listing it again
#     here makes sdist contents independent of that backend behavior.
#   - LICENSE is NOT auto-included by ``license = { text = "Apache-2.0" }``
#     in modern setuptools — that key only sets metadata, it doesn't
#     copy a file. (PEP 639 ``license-files = ["LICENSE"]`` would, but
#     we're not on that yet.) So LICENSE ships ONLY because it's
#     listed here (sdist) and in package-data (wheel).
#   - CHANGELOG.md and RELEASING.md have no auto-include path; listed
#     here is the only way they make it into the sdist.
#
# If you remove any of these lines, ``twine check`` will still pass
# but ``tar tzf dist/*.tar.gz`` will be silently missing files.
include LICENSE
include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include RELEASING.md

# Belt-and-suspenders: keep build leftovers and old sdist extractions
# out of the next sdist build.
prune dist
prune build
prune *.egg-info
prune opennvr_adapter_sdk-*
